{
 "name": "R1-03-core-ignores-second-own-leave",
 "note": "bea leaves her member grant twice: L1 (cut at L1 itself), then L2 (a later block of hers, counted_to = her own acceptance). circles.md: where more than one authorised stop ends a grant, a block must be within every cut, so her note signed as the circle after the acceptance is outside L2's cut and speaks for no one. Oracle: may_act_as false and removed[bea] = the acceptance. Core: ignores L2 (a stop by someone who is no longer a member goes through `can(..)` and is dropped, fold.rs:1182-1184, `own` is false once the grant has ended because `who` is read from non-ended heads; the stop then fails `can(..)` and is skipped, so its cut never reaches stop_cuts nor `ends`), so may_act_as is true and removed[bea] = null.",
 "steps": 8,
